From a3d06921ce7506e56eb9b3444a70dbbe9c69cac4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Neill Kapron <nkapron@google.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 22:49:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: fuse-bpf: fix verifier bypass in
 fuse_prog_is_valid_access

Enforce read-only access for out_args[i].value in
fuse_prog_is_valid_access() to prevent verifier bypass and arbitrary
kernel writes/frees.

Fixes: be926e6761d2 ("ANDROID: fuse-bpf: fuse-bpf v1.3")
Bug: 508702133
Assisted-by: Antigravity:gemini-3.1-pro
Signed-off-by: Neill Kapron <nkapron@google.com>
Cherrypick-From: https://android-review.googlesource.com/q/commit:5c7556339e29dd5f140bcd61b505922ecd180b10
Merged-In: I9a913a95a9695e92adbcffbbaca175815a55d948
Change-Id: I9a913a95a9695e92adbcffbbaca175815a55d948
Signed-off-by: Neill Kapron <nkapron@google.com>
---
 kernel/bpf/bpf_fuse.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/bpf_fuse.c b/kernel/bpf/bpf_fuse.c
index c6aa670bc54c13..992eb2dd5aa673 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/bpf_fuse.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/bpf_fuse.c
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@ static bool fuse_prog_is_valid_access(int off, int size,
 		if (off == offsetof(struct fuse_bpf_args, out_args[i].value)) {
 			info->reg_type = PTR_TO_BUF;
 			info->ctx_field_size = 256;
+			if (type != BPF_READ)
+				return false;
 			return true;
 		}
 	}
